Staleness at the point of use is the column teams forget. Data refreshed nightly and consulted at 4pm is up to 16 hours old at the moment a decision depends on it.

## Identity rules

**Get this wrong and every downstream join is wrong**, in a way that surfaces months later and is expensive to unwind. State it explicitly even when it seems obvious.

| Entity | Minted by | Referenced by | Key | Key stable? | On disagreement |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| | | | | | survivorship / adjudicator |

Ingestion must run in identity order — the minting system first. This is a hard dependency.

